      "target": "../sections/sec-000-acknowledgements.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The World Health Organization (WHO) gratefully acknowledges the contributions of many \nindividuals and organizations to these guidelines for the use of long-acting injectable cabotegravir \nfor HIV prevention.\nGuideline Development Group\nCo-chairs: Elizabeth Irungu (Jhpiego, Kenya) and Danvic Rosadiño (LoveYourself, Philippines).\nMax Appenroth (Global Action for Trans Equality, Germany), Connie Celum, (University of \nWashington, United States of America (USA)), Mohamed Chakroun (University Hospital Monastir, \nTunisia), Thato Chidarikire (National Department of Health, South Africa), Olga Denisi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Acknowledges contributors to the guidelines on long-acting injectable cabotegravir, naming the Guideline Development Group co-chaired by Elizabeth Irungu and Danvic Rosadiño and other members, reviewers and WHO staff. It notes funding from PEPFAR, USAID, Unitaid and the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation.",
        "state": "draft",
