    {
      "id": "library/10665-360869/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Purpose",
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 11,
      "target": "../sections/sec-004-purpose.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Achieving the Global AIDS target for 2025 of ensuring that 95% of people at risk of HIV \nacquisition have access to HIV prevention options requires a focus on expanding effective HIV \nprevention choices. Pre-exposure prophylaxis (PrEP) is a key component of combination HIV \nprevention. In 2015 the World Health Organization (WHO) recommended oral PrEP containing \ntenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF) for people at substantial risk of HIV (1) and, in 2021, \nrecommended the dapivirine vaginal ring (DVR) for cisgender women at substantial risk of HIV \n(2). Although expansion of access to and uptake",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that reaching the 2025 target of 95% access to HIV prevention requires more prevention choices, recalling WHO's 2015 oral PrEP and 2021 dapivirine ring recommendations and slow uptake. It presents the guideline's purpose of recommending long-acting cabotegravir using a public health approach and highlighting implementation considerations.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-360869/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Guideline development methodology",
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 12,
      "target": "../sections/sec-005-guideline-development-methodology.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "In response to the availability of new evidence on the efficacy of CAB-LA for the prevention \nof HIV acquisition, external experts and stakeholders proposed to make this recommendation \nas an addition to the HIV prevention recommendations in the 2021 Consolidated guidelines on \nHIV prevention, testing, treatment, service delivery and monitoring (3).\nAs a result, from January to May 2022, the WHO Department of Global HIV, Hepatitis and \nSexually Transmitted Infections Programmes led the development of new guidance with \nsupport from a Guideline Development Group (GDG) and an External Review Gro",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes how the cabotegravir recommendation was developed between January and May 2022 by WHO with a Guideline Development Group and External Review Group, based on a PICO question and systematic reviews. It states that the group judged the evidence of moderate certainty and unanimously made a conditional recommendation to offer long-acting cabotegravir as an additional prevention choice.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-360869/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Implications for implementation",
      "pageStart": 12,
      "pageEnd": 13,
      "target": "../sections/sec-006-implications-for-implementation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "CAB-LA should be delivered as an additional \nchoice alongside other PrEP options, \nincluding oral PrEP and the DVR, as part of a \ncomprehensive HIV prevention approach. To \ndate, provision of CAB-LA has largely been \nlimited to trial settings, certain geographies \nand specific populations. This guideline \noutlines operational research needed to \naddress research and implementation gaps, and to inform decisions on how to approach the \nimplementation and scale-up of CAB-LA successfully. The GDG stressed that operational \nresearch – and implementation of services itself – must involve the full pa",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "States that long-acting cabotegravir should be offered alongside oral PrEP and the dapivirine ring within comprehensive prevention, noting that provision has so far been mostly limited to trials. It lists implementation considerations and research needs, such as HIV testing strategies, service delivery models, drug resistance, safety in pregnancy and cost-effectiveness, with full community participation.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
